    <string name="cloud_disclosure_action_enable">Agree and enable</string>
    <string name="cloud_disclosure_footer">Cancel keeps cloud attestation disabled. You can turn it off from L3 at any time.</string>
    <string name="cloud_disclosure_content">Information sent\n\n1. A fresh Key Attestation certificate chain generated with a random alias for this challenge, plus Android version, system/vendor/boot patch levels, and Root of Trust data parsed from TEE extensions.\n\n2. The local L0–L2 report, including layer status, findings, app version, scan duration, and device baseline. Release builds do not upload full debug evidence.\n\n3. Device and ROM metadata: brand, manufacturer, model, product, device codename, board, SKU, Android and build versions, security patch, build time, ABIs, and build fingerprint.\n\n4. SoC and platform identifiers, including hardware platform, SoC model, vendor, supported ABIs, plus kernel version, build identity, and architecture obtained through the project’s existing mechanism.\n\n5. Boot and VBMeta state, including lock state, Verified Boot, verity mode, and the VBMeta digest when available.\n\nPurpose\n\nThis information is used to identify leaked or revoked keyboxes, compare TEE data with userspace properties, validate device and vendor metadata, verify SoC/platform combinations, assess Android/kernel version compatibility, and return a server-signed risk verdict. Detection rules can be updated in the cloud.\n\nNetwork and privacy\n\nData is sent to api.lingqing.ltd over HTTPS. Cloudflare, network operators, and related infrastructure may process connection metadata such as IP address, request time, and routing as part of Internet communication. This feature is not designed to read contacts, messages, photos, precise location, phone number, or IMEI, but certificates and system identifiers may form stable device characteristics. Turning cloud attestation off prevents future automatic cloud-attestation requests.</string>
